      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "CHANGES vs. ORIGINAL",
      "fontSize": 22,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "CHANGES vs. ORIGINAL",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "G4dxAuiWZ4l-v5ekKk8n",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1800,
      "y": 280,
      "width": 662.48,
      "height": 315.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1452290945,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 503060120,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791427462440,
      "created": 1791427462440,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Elasticsearch removed. Postgres full-text search is proportionate at ~50k URLs;\n   step up to Meilisearch/Typesense only if a concrete query needs it.\n2. In-memory 'has visited' tracker -> Postgres UNIQUE index. Survives restarts,\n   so a crash never re-pays Jev / judge calls for the same page.\n3. Doctor process -> systemd Restart= plus a heartbeat row per sweeper shown in admin.\n4. LLM master judge stays on the crawler VM as its own small service: it is an API\n   wrapper with near-zero CPU/RAM, and one per VM is the natural place for its rate cap.\n5. Raw pages become content-addressed zstd blobs in Postgres (sha256 PK). One store,\n   one backup, transactional link to findings. Move to files on block storage past ~100 GB.\n6. Queue drawn explicitly. Per-host leases keep the CLI's politeness guarantees\n   (robots, --delay-ms) intact across N workers.\n7. Data VM has no public interface. Admin is behind auth on the private network.\n8. 'Chosen reports' becomes an explicit published flag, so nothing about a third-party\n   site reaches the public site without a review step.\n9. Durability = nightly pg_dump to a Hetzner Storage Box, off-provider. Losing the Data VM\n   costs at most one day. No object storage bill, no second store to keep consistent.\n10. No Kubernetes. Crawlers are stateless and coordinate through the Postgres queue, so\n   scaling out is one more VM, or resizing this one. Est. ~$93/mo as drawn (~$0.14/hr).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Elasticsearch removed. Postgres full-text search is proportionate at ~50k URLs;\n   step up to Meilisearch/Typesense only if a concrete query needs it.\n2. In-memory 'has visited' tracker -> Postgres UNIQUE index. Survives restarts,\n   so a crash never re-pays Jev / judge calls for the same page.\n3. Doctor process -> systemd Restart= plus a heartbeat row per sweeper shown in admin.\n4. LLM master judge stays on the crawler VM as its own small service: it is an API\n   wrapper with near-zero CPU/RAM, and one per VM is the natural place for its rate cap.\n5. Raw pages become content-addressed zstd blobs in Postgres (sha256 PK). One store,\n   one backup, transactional link to findings. Move to files on block storage past ~100 GB.\n6. Queue drawn explicitly. Per-host leases keep the CLI's politeness guarantees\n   (robots, --delay-ms) intact across N workers.\n7. Data VM has no public interface. Admin is behind auth on the private network.\n8. 'Chosen reports' becomes an explicit published flag, so nothing about a third-party\n   site reaches the public site without a review step.\n9. Durability = nightly pg_dump to a Hetzner Storage Box, off-provider. Losing the Data VM\n   costs at most one day. No object storage bill, no second store to keep consistent.\n10. No Kubernetes. Crawlers are stateless and coordinate through the Postgres queue, so\n   scaling out is one more VM, or resizing this one. Est. ~$93/mo as drawn (~$0.14/hr).",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    }
  ],
